          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5857.71527336401,
            "y": 6141.191822323958
          },
          "code": "ANALYZE_USER_INPUT",
          "id": "1772142220001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772142220002_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a classifier.\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTask:\nAnalyze the input and return exactly ONE of these values:\n\nCRITICALTALENT\nCOVERAGE\n\nClassification Rules\n\nReturn CRITICALTALENT if the input is asking about:\ncritical talent\ncritical employee(s)\nlikely to leave employee(s)\nhigh-risk employee(s)\nhigh-impact employee(s)\nat-risk employee(s)\nimpact of loss\nrisk of loss\njob risk\nperformance (rating)\npotential (rating)\nkey role(s)\nteam health\norganization-wide critical talent\nsuccession plans\nsuccessors\nsuccession coverage within a manager's team\ndirect reports with or without successors\nsuccession plans needing attention\nsuccession plans at risk\nsuccession plans with successors\nsuccession plans without successors\nsuccession plans under a specific employee or manager\n\nReturn COVERAGE if the input is asking about replacement, backfill, or transition coverage, including:\nreplace\nreplacement for\nbackfill\nbackup for\nwho can replace\nwho could replace\nwho will replace\nwhat happens if leaves\nwhat happens if retires\nwhat happens if is promoted\nif leaves\nif retires\nif quits\nretirement\npromotion\nmoves out of role\n\nPriority Rule\n\nIf both CRITICALTALENT and COVERAGE match or neither of the rules matches, return CRITICALTALENT.\n\nOutput Rules\n\nReturn only one value.\nDo not explain your reasoning.\nDo not return JSON.\nDo not return any additional text.\nIf no rule matches, return EMPTY.\nMatching must be case-insensitive.\nTreat hyphenated and non-hyphenated forms as equivalent (e.g., \"high-risk\" = \"high risk\", \"at-risk\" = \"at risk\")."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userInput\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
