          "code": "EXTRACT_MANAGEMENT_LEVEL_AND_REQUESTED_TALENT_RATINGS",
          "id": "1765484480093",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765484480095_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract riskOfLoss, impactOfLoss, jobRisk, performance, potential, and managementLevel from {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}.\n\nReturn only valid JSON.\n\nOutput format:\n\n{\n\"riskOfLoss\": [],\n\"impactOfLoss\": [],\n\"jobRisk\": [],\n\"performance\": [],\n\"potential\": [],\n\"managementLevel\": 2\n}\n\nGeneral Rules\n\n* riskOfLoss, impactOfLoss, jobRisk, performance, and potential must always be arrays.\n* Array values must always be uppercase strings.\n* Allowed values:\n  * \"HIGH\"\n  * \"MEDIUM\"\n  * \"LOW\"\n* Never return duplicate values within an array.\n* Never return null.\n* Never return \"Unknown\".\n* Use an empty array when no value is requested.\n* Return only JSON.\n* Do not include explanations.\n* Do not include additional keys.\n\nManagement Level Rules\n\n* If the user explicitly mentions \"direct reports\", set managementLevel to 1.\n* If the user explicitly specifies a management level, use that value.\n* Otherwise set managementLevel to 2.\n\nImportant:\n\nThe following phrases affect managementLevel only and must NOT set any rating filters:\n\n* under [manager name]\n* manager's team\n* reports to\n* direct reports\n* team\n* organization\n* succession coverage\n\nRating Extraction Rules\n\nExtract requested values for:\n\n* riskOfLoss\n* impactOfLoss\n* jobRisk\n* performance\n* potential\n\nConvert all extracted values to uppercase.\n\nExamples:\n\n* high impact of loss\n  => impactOfLoss: [\"HIGH\"]\n\n* low impact of loss\n  => impactOfLoss: [\"LOW\"]\n\n* medium impact of loss\n  => impactOfLoss: [\"MEDIUM\"]\n\n* high or low impact of loss\n  => impactOfLoss: [\"HIGH\", \"LOW\"]\n\n* medium or high performance\n  => performance: [\"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\"]\n\nBoolean Logic Rules\n\nIf the user uses OR language, include all requested values.\n\nExamples:\n\n* high or low impact of loss\n* either high or low impact of loss\n* high impact of loss OR low impact of loss\n\nReturn:\n\n{\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\", \"LOW\"]\n}\n\nIf the user uses AND language, include the requested values in their respective arrays.\n\nExample:\n\n\"high impact of loss AND low risk of loss\"\n\nReturn:\n\n{\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"],\n\"riskOfLoss\": [\"LOW\"]\n}\n\nCritical / At-Risk Rules\n\nIf the user asks about:\n\n* critical employees\n* critical talent\n* at-risk employees\n* at-risk talent\n* employees who are critical\n* employees at risk\n* who is critical\n* which employees are critical\n* which employees are at risk\n\nThen return:\n\n{\n\"riskOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"],\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"],\n\"jobRisk\": [\"HIGH\"]\n}\n\nLikely To Leave Rules\n\nIf the user asks about:\n\n* likely to leave employees\n* employees likely to leave\n* who is likely to leave\n* employees at risk of leaving\n* flight risk employees\n\nThen return:\n\n{\n\"riskOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"]\n}\n\nCombination Rules\n\nWhen the user specifies explicit values, use only the values requested.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"employees with high impact of loss\"\n\n{\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"]\n}\n\n\"employees with Low or high impact of loss\"\n\n{\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"LOW\", \"HIGH\"]\n}\n\n\"employees with High impact of loss and Low risk of loss\"\n\n{\n\"impactOfLoss\": [\"HIGH\"],\n\"riskOfLoss\": [\"LOW\"]\n}\n\nDefault Behavior\n\nIf the user does not request any rating filter:\n\n{\n\"riskOfLoss\": [],\n\"impactOfLoss\": [],\n\"jobRisk\": [],\n\"performance\": [],\n\"potential\": [],\n\"managementLevel\": <determined value>\n}\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\n\"Show employees under James Douglas\"\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n\"riskOfLoss\": [],\n\"impactOfLoss\": [],\n\"jobRisk\": [],\n\"performance\": [],\n\"potential\": [],\n\"managementLevel\": 2\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"managementLevel\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"riskOfLoss\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"impactOfLoss\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"jobRisk\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"performance\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"potential\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
