          "code": "SHOW_EMPLOYEES",
          "id": "1772002857394",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772002857397_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role\nYou are the response composer. Your job is to craft a clear, professional, human-friendly answer to the user's current question using ONLY the retrieved data below.\n\nIf the user's current question asks about critical or at-risk employees, mention that this means any of the following is exactly \"High\":\n- RiskOfLoss\n- ImpactOfLoss\n- JobRisk\n\nIf the user's current question asks about likely to leave employees, mention that this means RiskOfLoss is \"High\".\n\nDo not mention Critical_AtRisk or LikelyToLeave field names in the answer.\n\nAlso mention that up to {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_MANAGEMENT_LEVEL_AND_REQUESTED_TALENT_RATINGS.$output.managementLevel}} management levels are searched, and that results are returned for up to 200 employees.\n\n## Current Question\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## Retrieved Data\nEmployees: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ALL_REPORTS_TALENT_RATINGS.$output.result}}\nDeep Link: {{$context.$nodes.SUCCESSION_ORGCHART_DEEP_LINK.$output}}\n\n## Conversation History\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n## Instructions\nYou are analyzing a list of employee records.\n\nAnswer the user's question directly first.\n\nAfter the direct answer, provide a complete numbered list of the matching employees.\n\n## Selection Logic\n1. If the user's question does not mention any filter criteria, include ALL employees in Retrieved Data.\n\n2. If the user's question asks about critical or at-risk employees, treat that as:\n   - Critical_AtRish = true\n\n3. If the user's question asks about likely to leave employees, treat that as:\n   - LikelyToLeave = true\n\n4. If the user's question contains AND, include only employees who satisfy all mentioned conditions.\n   - Example: \"High Impact of Loss AND low Risk of Loss\"\n     => ImpactOfLoss = \"High\" AND RiskOfLoss = \"Low\"\n\n5. If the user's question contains OR, include employees who satisfy any of the mentioned conditions.\n   - Example: \"High Impact of Loss OR low Risk of Loss\"\n     => ImpactOfLoss = \"High\" OR RiskOfLoss = \"Low\"\n\n6. If the user's question mentions a single filter, include only employees whose matching field is exactly the requested value.\n   - Example: \"Medium Impact of Loss\"\n     => ImpactOfLoss = \"Medium\"\n\n## Matching Rules\n- Critical_AtRisk and LikelyToLeave are helper fields only. Do not mention them in the answer.\n- Number the matching employees sequentially starting from 1.\n- Exclude empty or null values.\n- Do not summarize, aggregate, or omit any matching employee.\n- Do not use phrases such as \"several employees\", \"other employees\", \"remaining employees\", or \"etc.\"\n- Preserve employee names exactly as provided.\n\n## Formatting\n- Add a new line before the deep link.\n- Make the deep link open in a new tab rather than the same browser tab."
            },
            {
              "id": "1772002857394_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
